## Install The Generator

```sh
npm install -g @bakingrl/create-plugin
```

This installs:

- `create-bakingrl-plugin`;
- `bakingrl-plugin`.

## Create A Package

```sh
create-bakingrl-plugin my-plugin
cd my-plugin
npm install
npm run build
npm run validate
```

The default template creates a trusted v4 package with a `runtime.node` entry
and V4 contribution metadata.

Other templates:

```sh
create-bakingrl-plugin my-overlay --template overlay-plugin
create-bakingrl-plugin my-native --template native-sidecar-plugin
```

## Development Loop

1. Edit `src/extension/index.ts`, browser entries, manifest contributions, or
   sidecar code.
2. Run `npm run build`.
3. Run `npm run validate`.
4. Run `npm run install:local`.
5. Reload packages in BakingRL or restart the app when testing extension host
   lifecycle behavior.

## Install Target

The helper installs into the BakingRL package directory:

- macOS: `~/Library/Application Support/com.quillianne.bakingrl/packages`
- Linux: `$XDG_DATA_HOME/com.quillianne.bakingrl/packages`
- Windows: `%LOCALAPPDATA%/com.quillianne.bakingrl/packages`

Set `BAKINGRL_PACKAGES_DIR` to override the target during development.

## Test In BakingRL

1. Start BakingRL from the host repository.
2. Open the Packages or Developer area.
3. Enable the package.
4. Open contributed visuals or host-owned settings.
5. Add contributed visuals to an overlay/editor layout.
6. Use diagnostics, logs, and runtime restart controls when testing crashes or
   activation behavior.

